                 DIGITAL TO TRANSITION ITS PC DIRECT
                   U.S. OPERATIONS TO PCs COMPLEAT


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 1, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced that it is moving its U.S. PC catalog and telesales 
operation to PCs Compleat.  As part of the agreement, the company is 
authorized to resell Digital's entire line of personal computers.  
The Marlborough, Massachusetts-based company will also produce and 
distribute Digital PC catalogs by PCs Compleat to end users. 

     Under terms of the agreement to be completed by June 19, PCs 
Compleat will offer employment to the approximately 60 employees 
affected in Digital's Merrimack, New Hampshire facility.  Existing 
Digital PC catalog 800 phone numbers will also be serviced by the 
new PCs Compleat employees.  The Digital PC catalog by PCs Compleat 
represents an expansion to the current PCs Compleat catalogs.

     "For the past 18 months, the Digital PC business has been 
moving from a direct to an indirect sales model," said Michael 
Pocock, Americas sales vice president, Personal Computer Business 
Unit.  "In 1993, about 80 percent of our business was handled by 
Digital selling directly to corporations.  Today, a majority of our 
PC business is handled by our partners: resellers, distributors, and 
systems integrators in the United States.  The addition of PCs 
Compleat helps move us closer to our goal of selling through 
partners wherever possible."

     PCs Compleat was chosen because it is successful selling to 
small and medium sized businesses and the company can smoothly take 
over the servicing of Digital PC's thousands of catalog customers.  
"Another important consideration in selecting PCs Compleat," 
explained Pocock, "was their willingness to not only employ the 
affected employees but also open an office in the Merrimack area."

     Gordon Hoffstein, chairman and chief executive officer of PCs 
Compleat said, "This arrangement represents a tremendous opportunity 
for all involved.  We add an experienced and successful sales and 
marketing organization as well as a new line of PCs from notebooks 
to desktops and servers.  Together we will continue to build 
Digital's brand recognition in the direct channel."  Hoffstein 
added, "Digital products are an integral part of  our company's 
strategy to be the premier direct source for personal computer 
products and services."

Background on Digital and PCs Compleat

     Hoffstein, Jack Littman-Quinn, president and chief operating 
officer, and William C. Brown, executive vice president, co-founded 
PCs Compleat in 1991.  Hoffstein had previously founded micro-
computer distributor, Microamerica which merged with Softsel in 1990 
and later became Merisel.

     PCs Compleat is the nation's leading super direct source for 
brand name personal computer products and services.  The company has 
won PC/Computing's Five Star customer service award, CIO magazine's 
Esprit award for information systems, and Merrin Information 
Services' Channelmarker Lighthouse award for automated systems that 
exceed the expectations of customers and vendors. With centralized 
facilities in Marlborough, Mass., PCs Compleat is redefining reseller 
standards for brands, price, delivery, and service.

     Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit offers notebooks, 
desktops/deskside systems, and servers through resellers, 
distributors, systems integrators, and direct from Digital.  Digital 
PC has doubled unit shipments each of the past three calendar years 
and was ranked by Dataquest as number 11 worldwide in 1994.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
