                  DIGITAL STRENGTHENS LEADERSHIP IN
              $439 MILLION LINE MATRIX PRINTER MARKET


       Announces LGO4plus Printer with Highest Reliability and
          Price/Performance, and the Powerful Multiprotocol
                      RapidPrint 200 Interface



MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 1, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced the LGO4plus line printer, a 467 lpm (line per minute) 
printer featuring the highest quality output and lowest cost-per-
page in its class.  Designed for heavy duty environments such as 
manufacturing, warehousing and distribution, the LGO4plus line 
matrix printer has unsurpassed reliability with a duty cycle, more 
than four times that of any competitor's product.  The line printer 
also provides leading network connectivity, offering ANSI, 
Proprinter, Epson, Printronix P Series and optional PGL or VGL to 
provide support for Alpha, PC and multi-user UNIX environments. 

     Digital also announced the easy-to-install RapidPrint 200 
Ethernet printer interface, a powerful multiprotocol interface that 
is capable of supporting up to printers.  The RapidPrint 200 
interface supports all types of parallel interfaces and 
bi-directional communication modes, allowing existing printer to be 
used to their fullest capabilities.  It supports Centronics, 
Dataproducts, Bi-Tronics and IEEE 1284 parallel modes, providing 
flexibility, compatibility and investment protection.  The 
RapidPrint 200 interface is supported by all Digital desktop and 
network printers, including the LGO4plus printer, as well as 
printers featuring serial and parallel ports.

     "Digital is committed to leveraging its technical expertise in 
the manufacture of cost-effective, high-quality, open printing 
solutions that meet the rapidly expanding needs of network users,"  
said Jeb Hurley, director of marketing and business operations for 
Digital's Printer Line of Business.  "With an unlimited duty cycle 
and connections to most any network, the LGO4plus printer is ideal 
for mission critical tasks, such as printing invoices and payroll 
documents."

     "The RapidPrint 200 interface extends the access of high 
duty-cycle printers like the LGO4plus line printer, to every user on 
networks supporting PC and Macintosh computers, UNIX, ULTRIX or VMS 
workstations, VT and VXT terminals, or a combination of all of 
them," said Bill Mello, marketing manager, Digital's Hub Business 
Group.  "With its ability to operate in UNIX, ULTRIX, OpenVMS and 
Alpha environments, the RapidPrint 200 interface is another example 
of Digital's expanding capabilities in open computing."

LGO4plus Line Matrix Printer -- Unsurpassed Price/Performance 

     Lowest cost of ownership in its class, quality output, 
durability and ease of maintenance combine to provide the LGO4plus 
printer with the best price/performance in its class.  For users who 
print both text and graphics, the LGO4plus printer provides an 
economical alternative to laser printers at about one-fifth the cost 
per page.  The all steel-constructed LGO4plus printer is capable of 
printing quality output around the clock, with minimal power 
consumption.  

     Targeted at applications such as invoices, statements, checks 
and bar code labels, the LGO4plus line printer is the first line 
matrix printer has the flexibility to handle a multitude of tasks.  
And, whether large character, graphics or traditional text, the 
printer delivers the highest quality output.  In addition, the 
design of the LGO4plus printer allows for easy accessibility to 
items, such as paper and ribbons, simplifying maintenance tasks.

     "Pioneer Standard is impressed by how neatly the LGO4plus 
printer manages our green bar paper supply and how quietly it 
prints," explained Laura Falasco, cost control analyst, Pioneer 
Standard Electronics, a distributor of electronics and test site for 
the LGO4plus printer.  "We're considering the purchase of this unit 
as a permanent fixture in the Cost Control Department."

RapidPrint 200 Ethernet Printer Interface -- Enhancing Connectivity

     The easy to install RapidPrint 200 interface, designed to be 
placed in any convenient location near the printer, provides direct 
access to AppleTalk, Novell NetWare, TCP/IP and LAT networks.  It 
supports 50Kbytes/sec to the printer, approximately five times 
faster than existing network print server devices.  In addition, the 
RapidPrint 200 interface operates at up to 115.2K baud and is 
equipped with its own power supply, connection cables, fastener kit, 
and utility diskette containing OpenVMS set-up program and on-line 
documentation.  

Pricing and Availability

     Suggested list price for the LGO4plus line matrix printer is 
$5,599.  The RapidPrint 200 Ethernet printer interface  has a 
suggested list price of $995.  Both are now available through 
Digital's worldwide network of reseller and distributor partners.  
For more information within the U.S. call 800-777-4343, or your 
authorized Digital representative.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
