             DIGITAL EXPANDS VENTURIS DESKTOP LINE WITH
                    HIGH PERFORMANCE PENTIUM PCs


        One of Industry's Most Extensive Line of Pentium PCs
                      Available in Volume Today


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 2, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
added high performance Pentium PCs to its Venturis line of easy-to-
use desktop systems for general business computing.  The new systems 
bring the price of Pentium PCs down to the level of high-end 486 
systems.  Starting at $1899, the six new Venturis systems greatly 
expand the price performance range available to a broad audience of 
personal computer users through Intel 75MHz, 90MHz and 100MHz 
Pentium processors.  

     Providing high reliability, top quality engineering, stylish 
ergonomic design and easy setup not typically found in volume-priced 
systems, the new Venturis line is the first in the industry to meet 
the new EPA Energy Star guidelines, designed to help users increase 
energy conservation.  In addition, the Venturis line provides DMI 
(Desktop Management Interface) support, making PCs easier to manage 
in both standalone and networked modes.  Digital supports DMI across 
all its commercial desktop PCs.  The Venturis line is also backed by 
Digital's experienced worldwide service and support organization, 
and a three-year limited warranty rated among the top in the 
industry.

     "Since its introduction last fall, Digital's Venturis line has 
achieved increased popularity as a feature-rich enterprise desktop 
system that offers ease-of-use and solid performance," said Howard 
Elias, vice president, Desktop Product Line for Digital's Personal 
Computer Business Unit.  "With today's announcement, the Venturis 
line broadens its appeal to a wider range of business users who 
count on performance, ease, and functionality, as well as price in 
determining value."

     "The new Venturis line is in the channel, in volume, and ready 
to ship," said Skip Gladfelter, vice president, Americas marketing 
for the PC Business Unit.  "They are the perfect complement to our 
successful Celebris line -- we now offer a Pentium price performance 
solution for every user's needs."

Leader in Energy Star Compliance

     The new Venturis models already meet the EPA's more stringent 
MOU V2.0 Energy Star requirements that will become effective on Oct. 
1, 1995.  By building future Energy Star compliance into the 
Venturis line a full six months early, Digital provides businesses 
with long-term investment protection as well as the immediate 
benefits of energy and cost savings by cutting energy consumption.  
In accordance with the future guidelines, the new systems ship with 
the power management settings enabled and a Windows-based user 
interface that allows users to customize their settings.  Also 
included are online tutorials and documentation describing the 
features and benefits of power management functions.

DMI Support for Desktops

     A founding member of the industry-wide consortium, DMTF 
(Desktop Management Task Force), Digital has played an active role 
in creating the DMI standard.  DMI is a standard application 
programming interface that handles the communication between network 
management applications and manageable products.  Whether standalone 
or linked to networks, Digital's DMI-ready systems are easy to use, 
understand, configure and manage.  Digital's DMI implementation for 
Venturis, Management Information Format, allows users and 
administrators to browse the system for information needed to 
perform asset management, status reporting, and other management 
functions via an easy-to-use Windows-based program.

     Building on Digital's strengths in networking, the new Venturis 
systems can be managed within Novell and Microsoft networking 
environments.  As a Windows for Workgroup client, the Venturis line 
supports enterprise network management tools such as Digital's 
POLYCENTER AssetWORKS and Microsoft's Systems Management Server 
(SMS).  To support the needs of departmental network administrators, 
the new Venturis systems support Intel's LANDesk and Digital's 
ManageWORKS network management tools.  In addition to DMI support 
for general business desktop systems, Digital supports DMI 
throughout the entire commercial desktop line.
 
Easy to Use, Easy to Maintain

     Based on feedback from customer focus groups, the Venturis line 
is Digital's first commercial desktop line to offer 'Quickstart DOS' 
and 'Quickstart Win' online documentation, helping users to become 
familiar with their PC.  In addition, animated tutorials are 
included for common systems functions such as printer setup and 
cabling, power management and using a CD-ROM. The Venturis systems 
also feature Plug and Play for unassisted system configuration and 
tool-free access to system internals to facilitate set-up, integration 
and maintenance.

High-End Features at Volume Prices

     The new models give users even greater latitude in choosing a 
desktop system that suits current -- and future -- processing, 
performance and connectivity requirements.  In addition to providing 
Pentium performance, the Venturis line now provides faster disk 
drives and larger storage capacity -- 420MB, 845MB and 1.2GB -- for 
greater configuration flexibility.  Venturis systems also will be 
equipped with Novell NetWare ready drivers for simplified 
networking.  PCMCIA and Infrared options provide seamless 
connectivity with Digital's mobile products. 

Pricing and Availability

     The new 'slimline' models -- Venturis 575, Venturis 590 and 
Venturis 5100 -- have U.S. list prices starting at $1899, $2249, and 
$2499, respectively.  The 'full profile' Venturis FP575, Venturis 
FP590 and Venturis FP5100 are housed in larger enclosures and have 
U.S. list prices starting at $1949, $2299 and $2549, respectively.  
All models are available in volume today.

     The systems come pre-installed with the Windows for Workgroups 
operating system and are designed to take advantage of Windows 95.  
The new Venturis PCs come with Digital's worldwide service and 
support through a limited three-year warranty, including one-year 
on-site, where available.  The systems are available through 
Digital's channel partners, including resellers, distributors and 
dealers, as well as through Digital's direct sales organization.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's marketplace.
