                    DIGITAL ANNOUNCES SUPPORT FOR
                      MICROSOFT SQL SERVER 6.0
            WITH THE INDUSTRY'S BROADEST LINE OF SERVERS

  
SAN FRANCISCO, Calif. -- May 2, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
is announcing support for Microsoft SQL Server 6.0 relational 
database management system with the industry's most complete and 
scalable CISC (Intel) and 64-bit RISC (Alpha) servers at this week's 
DB/EXPO '95 information technology conference.  In addition to 
platform support, Digital, as a Microsoft Solution Provider, will 
provide enterprise service and support for customers implementing 
Microsoft SQL Server 6.0 solutions.

     Digital's Windows NT Server and Microsoft BackOffice server 
platforms will all support the next version of Microsoft SQL Server, 
6.0.  With the industry's broadest range of server platforms, Digital 
is providing customers with flexibility and choice when deploying 
client-server solutions.  Digital's scalable server line-up for 
Window NT, from the Prioris Pentium based PC servers to the the 
AlphaServer 2100 systems with up to 4 Alpha microprocessors, will 
provide Microsoft SQL Server 6.0 customers an almost unlimited server 
growth path.  

     The Digital servers that will support Microsoft SQL Server 6.0 
include Prioris MTE systems; Prioris XL and HX servers; and 
AlphaServer 400 4/166, AlphaServer 1000 4/233, AlphaServer 2000 
4/233, AlphaServer 2000 4/275, AlphaServer 2100 4/233, AlphaServer 
2100 4/275, AlphaServer 2100 4/233 Rackmount, and AlphaServer 2100 
5/250 servers.

     "Digital provides the most comprehensive support for Microsoft 
SQL Server 6.0 in the industry," said Lucia Quinn, vice president of 
Digital's Windows NT Business Segment.  "With our scalable line of 
Digital Intel-based servers and AlphaServer systems, customers have 
the widest choice of servers to support Microsoft SQL Server 6.0.  
Digital also provides the enterprise support services required to 
implement and support these solutions."

     "Digital is a key player in providing both the platforms and 
enterprise service and support for Microsoft SQL Server 6.0," said 
Jim Allchin, senior vice president, Business Systems Division at 
Microsoft.  "Customers that have and will implement Microsoft SQL 
Server-based client-server solutions require the mission-critical 
platforms and service and support at a level that Digital provides."

Norwest Bank Enhances Customer Relationships

     Norwest Bank has implemented an advanced customer relationship 
management system for its commercial bankers based on Microsoft SQL 
Server running on Digital AlphaServer systems.  Norwest Bank, 
headquartered in Minneapolis, is part of the Norwest Corporation, and 
with $50 billion in assets, is one of the largest bank holding 
companies in the country.

     "With this system, Norwest has enhanced relationships with 
customers by enabling the bank to better identify and serve their 
needs.  This  has led to a 34 percent increase in commercial account 
fee revenue," said Daniel G. Pocrnich, senior vice president and 
chief financial officer of Norwest Bank Minnesota.  "We look forward 
to taking advantage of the new features of Microsoft SQL Server 6.0 
on scalable AlphaServers.  These features will allow us to continue 
growing our business by providing our banking professionals with easy 
access to information used to build productive relationships with 
customers."

Worldwide Enterprise Service, Support and Training

     Digital is a Microsoft Solution Provider Authorized Support 
Center with 29 support centers worldwide supporting over 450 field 
locations in over 100 countries.  Digital provides corporate 
customers using Microsoft products with the capabilities needed to 
implement and support mission-critical applications.  Digital has 
over 15,000 service professionals worldwide including 500 Microsoft 
Certified Professionals and over 5,000 Support Professionals trained 
on Microsoft products.

     To assist customers in building Microsoft SQL Server knowledge, 
Digital provides Microsoft SQL Server training as part of its' 
comprehensive Microsoft course offerings. Digital is a Microsoft 
Solution Provider Authorized Technical Education Center and is 
Microsoft's largest training partner with over 20,000 customers 
trained.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help organizations 
compete and win in today's global marketplace.
