           DIGITAL INTRODUCES NEW POLYCENTER SOFTWARE TOOL
           FOR OPTIMIZING THE PERFORMANCE OF DIGITAL UNIX


   ... keeps leadership Alpha systems running at their fastest...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 3, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced POLYCENTER Performance Advisor for Digital UNIX, a layered 
software product for tuning and optimizing Alpha system performance.  
>From a central location, POLYCENTER Performance Advisor analyzes 
system conditions and provides detailed recommendations for 
improving local and remote system operation, increasing user 
productivity and helping eliminate the need for additional 
equipment expenditures.

     "Even though Alpha systems running the Digital UNIX operating 
system have industry-leading performance, periodic tuning can keep 
them running at peak efficiency," said Ann Dinneen, product manager 
for Digital's performance management products. "Digital UNIX users 
will love this tool because it is easy to use, gives them tremendous 
insight into system operations, and can help them tune their Alpha 
systems to run even faster."

     POLYCENTER Performance Advisor for Digital UNIX builds on 
Digital's experience with three generations of performance 
management applications for OpenVMS.  In operation, a smart agent -- 
the POLYCENTER Performance Advisor Collector -- runs in the 
background collecting data and comparing it to rules and thresholds 
which can provide immediate alerts for critical performance 
conditions.  The POLYCENTER Performance Advisor polls the Collector 
and analyzes the data to quickly identify performance problems and 
potential bottlenecks.  

     Employing an expert-system knowledge base to evaluate system 
workload, the POLYCENTER Performance Advisor creates analysis and 
evaluation reports.  Analysis reports identify specific conditions 
causing performance degradation and make recommendations for 
improving system performance.  The evaluation reports help identify 
trends in system performance and assist in gauging the impact of 
changes in workload and configuration characteristics. 

Reports include:

     o 	CPU and memory usage
     o 	Disk utilization
     o 	Network activity
     o 	Paging and swapping
     o 	Process statistics
     o 	System level statistics
     o 	Tape activity

     In addition, POLYCENTER Performance Advisor can send 
customized, rule-based alarms to system and network management 
products such as POLYCENTER NetView and POLYCENTER Console Manager, 
as well as to other SNMP management applications.  

     The POLYCENTER Performance Advisor for Digital UNIX, V3.0, is 
priced at $3,000 for a concurrent use license and $10,000 for an 
unlimited system use license.  The POLYCENTER Performance Advisor 
Collector, required for each CPU, is priced at $1,000.  Both 
components are orderable now and will ship on May 30, 1995.

