                 TMN NETWORKS INC. SELECTS DIGITAL'S
                          MEDIA SERVER FOR
        CANADIAN DEPLOYMENT OF EXPANDED PROGRAMMING SERVICES

 
     Multi-Million Dollar Commitment Provides First Media Server
          Technology Solution For Deployment Of "Real-Time"
                 Pay-Per-View and Pay TV Programming

 
MAYNARD, Mass. -- April 26, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that TMN Networks Inc., the majority partner of 
Viewer's Choice Canada Pay Per View and the owner of TMN - The Movie 
Network and MOVIEPIX, has signed a multi-million dollar agreement to 
use Digital's second-generation media server technology for network 
origination of pay-per-view and pay television programming.  When 
the equipment is installed this fall, TMN Networks Inc. will be the 
world's first to deliver a complete broadcast schedule using MPEG-2 
digital compression. 

     As a result of the agreement, TMN Networks Inc. will be 
expanding its Viewer's Choice network from four channels to 20 
channels of pay-per-view programming via satellite by September. 
Digital's media server technology replaces conventional videotape 
machines for network origination of pay-per-view and pay television, 
allowing TMN Networks Inc. to add more channels cost-effectively in 
the future. 

     According to Lisa de Wilde, president of TMN Networks Inc., 
"Digital understands TMN's business and the operational issues 
involved in our programming expansion.  Our deal with Digital will 
facilitate operations for all the networks, achieving higher quality 
-- and for Viewer's Choice, permitting 'real-time' satellite 
delivery and increased channel capacity." 

     DeWilde added, "The networks' objective is to shine as the 
commercial-free, in-home movie destination for Eastern Canada.  
Digital brings to us the best technological expertise available to 
accomplish our goal of delivering greater choice and convenience in 
movies and special events, with laser disk-quality video and 
CD-quality sound." 

     "TMN Networks will be using the Digital media server to deliver 
Near Video-On-Demand (NVOD) for Viewer's Choice Pay Per View, as 
well as originate their five premium channels," said Frank Foley, 
Digital's business development manager for cable television.  "While 
TMN Networks' implementation is commercial-free, this is the same 
platform Digital uses for commercial ad insertion, demonstrating the 
flexibility of our server architecture." 

     Foley added, "This sends a message to the industry that you can 
buy a media server from Digital for NVOD, expand it to insert ads, 
and grow it further to support interactive applications." 

     Digital's media server technology has already been selected by 
more cable and telephone companies worldwide than any other media 
server provider.  The company's Video and Interactive Information 
Services Architecture (VIIA) provides a full-service solution for 
delivering interactive video applications over many types of 
networks.  Digital's platform features object-oriented middleware 
that links the world's fastest server systems -- based on 64-bit 
Alpha processors -- with the company's StorageWorks disk arrays and 
digital tape library systems.  VIIA also provides network, 
subscriber and billing management capabilities, including full 
compatibility with existing tools. 

     TMN Networks Inc. is owned by Montreal's Astral Communications 
Inc., an integrated Canadian communications company providing 
innovative consumer- oriented broadcasting (including pay television 
and specialty services, in both English and French, and Viewer's 
Choice Pay Per View), entertainment and related retail services. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry 
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
