              DIGITAL SPEEDS UP ALPHASERVER 1000 SYSTEM


          Most Reliable Low-End Server with Full Clustering



MAYNARD, Mass. -- April 24, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today increased the processing power of its AlphaServer 1000 system 
by incorporating a faster 233 MHz CPU. The enhanced system is the 
same price as its predecessor, the AlphaServer 1000 4/200 server. 

     The AlphaServer 1000 4/233 server is a uniprocessor server in a 
deskside tower enclosure and supports up to 512 MBytes of memory and 
440 GBytes of total storage. Its large memory and storage 
capacities, combined with an even faster Alpha CPU, allow the server 
to deliver large-system performance of up to an estimated 850 
transactions per minute (TPM) at small-system prices. The system 
delivers even higher levels of performance and availability when 
used as part of a cluster. 

     "In today's competitive environment, users are constantly being 
asked to do more, faster, and at less cost. They require inexpensive 
yet reliable systems with quick response times," said Philippe 
Ribeyre, vice president of Digital's Low End Server group. "The 
AlphaServer 1000 4/233 server is cost-effective for PC LANs, 
database applications, and as an applications and Internet server.

     "It is also the industry's most reliable low-cost server with 
full clustering. Clustering allows a group of systems to be managed 
as a single system and provides extremely high data and applications 
availability through redundant CPUs, storage, and data paths. 
Digital was a pioneer in the development of clusters and today, no 
other computer vendor offers full clustering in a server at this 
price." 

Maximum Uptime

     The server contains many other high reliability features for 
business-critical applications so users have the lowest possible 
risk of downtime. Built-in sensors monitor the server, and the LCD 
control panel indicates system status at a glance. Any problems can 
be handled remotely, without interrupting other activities. Hot swap 
drives are also available and allow users to replace a disk while 
the rest of the system continues to operate.

     The AlphaServer 1000 4/233 system also offers fully redundant 
power supplies, a dual SCSI backplane, and ECC (error correction 
code) memory and cache. No other computer vendor offers as many high 
reliability features in a server at this price point. 

Outstanding Investment Protection

     The server comes with a three-year, onsite warranty with 
next-day response. Digital offers inexpensive system upgrades from 
MicroVAX and DECsystem servers to the new AlphaServer 1000 4/233 
server. Cost-effective CPU upgrades are also available for the 
AlphaServer 1000 4/200 server. 

Pricing and Availability

     The list price for an AlphaServer 1000 4/233 server with the 
Windows NT operating system, 64 MBytes of memory, 2 GBytes storage, 
a CD-ROM, and an Ethernet adapter is $15,970. The list price for an 
AlphaServer 1000 4/233 server with the Digital UNIX or OpenVMS 
operating systems, 64 MBytes of memory, 2 GBytes of storage, a 
CD-ROM, an Ethernet adapter, and NAS 200+ software is $17,980. 

     The AlphaServer 1000 4/233 server is also available in space 
savings rackmount configurations that fit into most 19-inch industry 
standard cabinets.  The AlphaServer 1000 4/233 server is available 
today.

