                NEW AdvantageCluster SYSTEMS FEATURE
                     SUPERIOR SYSTEM RELIABILITY


        ... Provide automatic failover for high availability
                    in commercial applications...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- April 27, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the newest members of its AdvantageCluster family of 
highly available servers. The new systems, the AdvantageCluster 
5004/275 and AdvantageCluster 5004/233 configurations are designed 
to meet the needs of commercial users who demand maximum system 
availability and low overall system cost. 

     "Digital introduced clusters in the mid-80's, said Pauline 
Nist, vice president of Digital's AlphaServer Business Segment. 
"This latest member of our AdvantageCluster family is based on our 
most popular mid-range server, and runs Digital UNIX(R), the most 
standards-compliant software available today."

     The new cluster systems, complete packages in a single cabinet, 
each comprise two AlphaServer 2100 nodes, expanded memory, 8Gbytes 
of disk storage, tape backup, and all necessary software. Each of 
the AlphaServer node can be expanded to four processors, and the 
cluster can be expanded to four AlphaServer 2100 computer nodes, for 
those applications which require high levels of compute performance 
along with high availability. 

     Digital's AdvantageCluster systems feature multiple processors 
each running independent workloads, and DECsafe Available Server 
software which continuously monitors operation of all processors and 
all nodes. In the event of a failure in one of the nodes, the 
remaining units pick up the application workload and provide 
continuous service to all users. 

     "Our experience shows that applications can resume processing 
in less than 30 seconds of a failure," said Nist. "The capability we 
have built into the AdvantageCluster Available Server family 
provides the uptime customers need for critical applications and the 
cost structure of off-the-shelf systems." 

Industry Leading Software Included

     The AdvantageCluster available server includes Digital's 
Logical Storage Manager, POLYCENTER Advanced File System, and 
DECsafe Available Server software, all running under Digital UNIX. 
These software components provide the flexible, shared storage 
environment, the rapid file recovery, and the system monitoring 
features which give customers over 99% availability in a standard, 
off-the-shelf system. 

     Two models are available: The AdvantageCluster 5004/233 
configuration, based on the AlphaServer 2100 4/233 computer is 
priced from $102,000. The AdvantageCluster 5004/275 system, based on 
the AlphaServer 2100 4/275 computer is priced from $127,000. Each is 
fully expandable to four nodes and each node can be expanded to four 
processors.

Designed for sale through Distributors and VARs

     "The new cluster system is specially packaged for distribution 
through Digital's channels partners," said Gene Nelson, vice 
president of Computer Special Systems. "By offering complete 
configurations, including multiple component computers, networking 
interface cards, cables, software, etc., a customer can order under 
one part number all the parts factory integrated and tested. Options 
can be added under another option number. This packaging assures 
proper configurations and keeps customer delivery time to under 30 
days." 

