          VERSION 1.3 OF PATHWORKS FOR OpenVMS (Macintosh)
                EXTENDS SUPPORT TO THE ALPHA PLATFORM


   ...new Macintosh-based server management capabilities simplify
                        NOS administration...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 5, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced version 1.3 of its PATHWORKS for Macintosh client and 
server software.  The PATHWORKS for OpenVMS server software is now 
available for the first time on Digital's performance-leading 64-bit 
Alpha RISC platform.  The new version of PATHWORKS for Macintosh 
includes enhanced server administration, a browser for the Internet 
Worldwide Web and new TCP/IP utilities, providing users with 
expanded capabilities for integrating and managing diverse desktop 
systems.  

     PATHWORKS for Macintosh clients have the ability to share 
applications, data, printers and resources, as well as access 
information from remote systems on the network.  Version 1.3 of 
PATHWORKS for Macintosh includes new management capabilities that 
allow a system manager to administer users, files, print queues and 
volumes on OpenVMS VAX and Alpha servers, all from a native 
Macintosh application.  The Mosaic browser provides  a graphical 
navigational tool to surf the Internet's Worldwide Web.  Also 
included in PATHWORKS for Macintosh is support for the TCP/IP V2.0.6 
transport from Apple, FTP and Telnet utilities, and a full DECnet 
Phase IV implementation.

     Servers running PATHWORKS for OpenVMS (Macintosh) version 1.3 
provide commercial-strength file, print and mail services, fully 
integrating networked Macintosh systems into the entire 
organization.   With version 1.3 running on the high-performance 
Alpha RISC platform, a single PATHWORKS for OpenVMS (Macintosh) 
server can offer a separate network zone for each workgroup or 
department, providing tailored lists of file and print services 
available to each group of users.  This feature cuts down on 
browsing time and makes it easier for users to find the volumes and 
printers they need.  In addition, PATHWORKS servers now support 
AppleTalk for OpenVMS V3.2.   

     Along with support for Alpha platforms, PATHWORKS for OpenVMS 
(Macintosh) version 1.3 also is available for VAX systems, with 
connectivity to Digital UNIX* systems provided through the Pacer for 
Digital UNIX solution.  The PATHWORKS for Macintosh client software 
lets Macintosh users access file, print and application services 
from an unlimited number of PATHWORKS and Pacer servers without 
modifications.

     PATHWORKS for Macintosh, V1.3 is available today.  The 
PATHWORKS for Macintosh client is priced at $250, and upgrades from 
existing PATHWORKS versions are priced at $99.  The PATHWORKS for 
OpenVMS (Macintosh) server access is included with the PATHWORKS for 
Macintosh client.

     PATHWORKS for Macintosh is a member of Digital's PATHWORKS 
family of networking and network integration solutions for local and 
wide-area networks.  PATHWORKS integrates the broadest set of PC and 
server platforms with the leading network technologies and network 
operating systems.  

PATHWORKS solutions are available for most popular platforms, 
including DOS, Windows, Windows NT, NetWare, LAN Manager, UNIX, 
OpenVMS and OS/2, and shortly for Windows 95.  

