         WESTMINSTER (UK) CABLE SIGNS CONTRACT WITH DIGITAL
           TO PROVIDE TECHNOLOGY FOR VIDEO-ON-DEMAND TRIAL
                       WITH CABLE TV CUSTOMERS


               First Truly Interactive Trial in London


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 5, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced that Westminster Cable, a London cable TV operator in the 
Borough of Westminster franchise, is implementing Digital Equipment 
Corporation's Mediaplex media server technology to provide a 
complete solution for a video-on-demand trial involving 100 
customers initially and expanding to 1000.

     The contract includes provisions for Digital's Mediaplex video 
server technology and systems integration expertise.

     The beta trial will run from November 1995 to March 1996, and 
will ultimately enable customers to choose from a constantly-updated 
video library of 200 titles.  British Telecom-owned Westminster 
Cable is the first to offer a truly interactive video-on-demand 
system in London.  Because Westminster's cable network is 
constructed using switched-star technology, the return path provides
a degree of interactivity unmatched by the traditional cable TV 
networks currently under construction.

     David Lethbridge, sales and marketing director at Westminster 
Cable, stated, "We are delighted to be working with Digital on this 
trial.  The company has unparalleled experience in this field, 
demonstrated by the fact that the Mediaplex platform has already 
been selected by many cable and TV companies worldwide.  The 
server's ease of operation and direct compatibility with our billing 
and management information systems is a major plus."

     Lethbridge added, "Westminster Cable has taken the lead in UK's 
cable TV industry with this move.  True video-on-demand, the ability 
to see what you want, when you want it, provides the ultimate in 
customer choice.  It will enable us to meet more closely the needs 
of the world's most culturally diverse cable TV franchise, in that 
it will give customers a real choice in their viewing."

     "Digital's and Westminster Cable's market-leading trial 
reinforces the growing worldwide interest in Digital's Mediaplex 
architecture," said Jacques Setton, Marketing Manager Europe of 
Digital's Video and Interactive Information Services.  "We are 
committed to providing the industry's most advanced capabilities at 
a low cost-per-stream."

     Digital's video server technology, now sold using the company's 
Mediaplex trademark, has already been selected by more cable and 
telephone companies worldwide than any other media server provider.  
The Mediaplex architecture provides a full-service solution for 
delivering interactive video applications over many types of 
networks. Digital's platform features object-oriented middleware 
that links the world's fastest server systems -- based on 64-bit 
Alpha processors -- with the company's StorageWorks disk arrays and 
digital tape library systems.  

     The Mediaplex architecture also provides network, subscriber 
and billing management capabilities, including full compatibility 
with existing tools.

     Established in 1983, Westminster Cable is a wholly-owned 
subsidiary of British Telecommunications plc. BT also has cable TV 
interests throughout the United Kingdom.  Westminster Cable offers 
viewers with the London Borough of Westminster a wide range of TV 
channels as well as the Reuters 1000 business information service 
via PC.  It was the first cable TV company in the UK to offer such a 
comprehensive business information package.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry 
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
