         DIGITAL EQUIPMENT SELECTS VELA RESEARCH AND PROBITA
           AS TECHNOLOGY PROVIDERS FOR MEDIAPLEX AD SERVER


     Technologies Enable Enhanced Video Resolution and Minimized
          Ad Insertion Operating Costs for Cable Companies


NCTA Conference, DALLAS, Texas -- May 8, 1995 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation announced it has chosen Vela Research, Inc. and Probita, 
Inc. to provide enabling technologies for its Mediaplex ad server, a 
scalable, digital video solution for cable advertising insertion.  
The result is an ad insertion system that offers price-performance 
leadership, complemented by high-quality video resolution, with an 
optional network management suite that further maximizes operating 
efficiencies for cable operators.

     "Digital's Mediaplex ad server enables cable companies to cut 
commercial insertion time from days to minutes, opening up new 
sources of revenue and generating cost savings," explained Peter 
Martin, Digital's Video and Interactive Information Service group's 
market manager for video advertising.

     "Customers using Digital's ad insertion system benefit today 
from Vela Research's high-quality MPEG-2 encoding/decoding.  They 
can also minimize operating costs by taking advantage of Probita's 
comprehensive network management environment.  With these offerings 
as part of the system, Digital clearly provides an unsurpassed 
solution for cable ad insertion," Martin added.

     Digital is using Vela Research's MPEG-2 Encoder, a digital 
compression processor ideally suited for the ad insertion 
environment, where advertising content is compressed and stored 
digitally for subsequent distribution and insertion on cable 
channels. Digital's ad insertion system also incorporates Vela 
Research's Model 2000-0201 EISA Decoder Board, an audio/video 
decoder designed for CATV headend decoding in Near Video-On-Demand 
and commercial ad insertion applications.

     As an option for its ad insertion customers, Digital is 
providing Probita's Proclaim multicast distribution and network 
management software.  Proclaim is optimized for distribution 
problems requiring enhanced network management, such as microwave, 
satellite, PSTN, or other specialized transport systems. Adlink's 
interconnect service, the second-largest cable ad insertion service 
in the U.S., relies on the Digital and Probita combination to 
provide highly efficient advertising distribution and network 
management critical for large, cable television interconnects.

     Digital's ad insertion system is based on the company's 
Mediaplex Architecture, which provides a comprehensive, standards-
based environment for delivering interactive video applications over 
many types of networks.  Digital's platform features object-oriented 
middleware that links the world's fastest server systems -- based on 
64-bit Alpha processors -- with the company's StorageWorks disk 
arrays and digital tape library systems.

     Vela Research Inc. is based in St. Petersburg, Florida. Vela's 
product lines include video servers, frame-only and adaptive field 
frame MPEG-2 encoders and several types of MPEG decoder boards.

     Probita, Inc. supplies custom software development, consulting, 
and broadband products and integration services for the cable 
television and telephony industries.  Based in Boulder, Colorado, 
Probita specializes in real-time, high-performance transaction 
systems and network command and control.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry 
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
