             DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION ANNOUNCES NEW
       DUAL-CONTROLLER CONFIGURATION AND INCREASED RAID LEVEL
          SUPPORT FOR STORAGEWORKS RAID ARRAY 410 SUBSYSTEM


  Strong Demand for Recently Introduced Raid Array Expected To Soar
        With Announcement of New Fault Tolerance Capabilities


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 12, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced new functionality and expanded platform support for 
the StorageWorks RAID Array 410, making it the highest performance, 
most reliable RAID subsystem available for multiplatform UNIX 
environments.  The RAID Array 410 now supports dual-controller 
configurations, allowing two controllers to be used with the same
subsystem, increasing system reliability and performance.  The dual-
controller configuration is rated at over 4,500 I/Os per second, 
making it today's fastest RAID subsystem.  Also new is controller-
based support for RAID level 1, providing a truly redundant RAID 
system that significantly increases data protection and availability 
without burdening the system CPU.  In addition, the RAID Array 410 
now supports Sun's Solaris 2.4 operating environment.

     "Dual-controller configurations provide StorageWorks RAID Array 
410 customers with outstanding performance and allow continuous 
operations in the unlikely event of controller failure," said Kirby 
Wadsworth, manager of StorageWorks product marketing. "This new high 
availability, high performance capability, coupled with extended RAID 
level support, will accelerate the already strong demand for the RAID 
Array 410.  Since our introduction of the RAID Array 410, just a few 
months ago, demand has already exceeded forecasts by more than 300%."

     Tom Flink, vice president of Vector Technology Corporation, a 
value-added reseller of workstations and servers in the UNIX market 
and an authorized integrator of StorageWorks products, added, "Our 
customers have responded very positively to the StorageWorks RAID 
Array 410 because of its superior performance, high reliability, 
robust fault tolerance and scalable, modular architecture.  These 
new enhancements, combined with the system's low price, make the 410 
an even more desirable product, consistent with the strong offerings 
in the StorageWorks product line."

StorageWorks RAID Array 410 -- High-Performance RAID For
Multiple UNIX Platforms

     Introduced in January 1995, the StorageWorks RAID Array 410 
provides reliable, expandable, cost-effective RAID storage for 
Hewlett-Packard, IBM, Sun's Solaris 2.3 and now, Solaris 2.4 
platforms.  With up to 4,500 I/O operations per second, and up 32 MB 
read- and write-back cache per controller, the RAID Array 410 is 
optimized to provide fast and highly reliable data access.  Because 
the product uses controller-based RAID, users can harness the power 
of computer systems for their applications, without unnecessary CPU 
overhead from I/O operations. New dual-controller integration and 
expanded RAID level support provides users with the highest 
performance and the highest levels of fault tolerance and data 
reliability available in the UNIX marketplace.  The modular 
architecture, snap-in, hot-swap components, and intuitive graphical 
user interface allow for easy installation, maintenance and expansion.

Pricing and Availability

     The StorageWorks RAID Array 410 Subsystem is priced lower than 
any comparable RAID product for UNIX at $23,642 for a 12.9 GB 
configuration, which consists of a StorageWorks six-channel SCSI 
controller with 32 MB read- and write-back cache, RAID software, and 
a StorageWorks office expansion enclosure with redundant fans and 
five optimized power supplies.  Dual-controller configurations of 
the RAID Array 410, which deliver increased performance and 
availability, start at $30,071.  The product is now available 
exclusively from select distributors and value-added resellers 
(VARs).  For more information about Digital's complete line of 
StorageWorks products, call 1-800-STORWORK (1- 800-786-9675).

     StorageWorks is a comprehensive family of disk, tape and 
optical storage subsystems, offering modular, competitively-priced, 
industry-standard solutions in customizable desktop, deskside, and 
datacenter enclosures.  StorageWorks products are available on 
multiple operating systems and hardware platforms, including Novell 
and Windows NT environments, plus Digital workstations and midrange 
computers, and Hewlett-Packard, IBM and Sun workstations and 
servers.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
