           DIGITAL AND OPEN ENVIRONMENT ANNOUNCE LICENSING
                   AGREEMENT FOR DCE ON WINDOWS NT

 
    ...agreement to expand availability of applications based on
              industry-standard middleware services...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 16, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation and 
Open Environment Corporation of Boston, Mass. today announced an 
agreement in which Open Environment will license Digital's DCE 
(Distributed Computing Environment) for Windows NT middleware 
software. Under the agreement, Open Environment will resell 
Digital's DCE software -- Runtime Services, Cell Directory Server 
and Security Server --  as part of its Entera Enterprise Operating 
Environment product line.  

     The Digital DCE software, based on the Open Software 
Foundation's (OSF) DCE, provides a basic infrastructure foundation 
which, together with the Entera development tools, will provide a 
robust enterprise operating environment for the Windows NT platform.  

     The agreement with Open Environment is the first to be 
announced by Digital for licensing the Windows NT version of DCE. 
The Digital DCE for Windows NT product set has been shipping since 
September, 1994 on both Intel and Alpha platforms and is integrated 
with the Microsoft RPC communication mechanism available in Windows 
NT.  

     "Digital believes that the Entera product line and Digital's 
DCE for NT will help Open Environment provide the best DCE-based 
solutions to their customers," according to Gerard van de Aast, 
group manager for Enterprise Software at Digital.  "This 
announcement is further proof that Digital is committed to partner 
with leading software providers for client/server solutions based on 
industry standards."

     "As a long-time business partner of Digital Equipment 
Corporation, we have witnessed the successful partnership they have 
cultivated in recent years with Microsoft and the Windows NT 
platforms," said Rod Hodgman, vice president of product marketing at 
Open Environment. "Open Environment believes that the Digital 
implementation of DCE for Windows NT will emerge as an important 
enterprise platform on which to base distributed applications."

     The Digital DCE products include the DCE Runtime Services, the 
DCE Developer's Kit, the DCE Security Server, and the DCE Cell 
Directory Server. Digital also offers DCE products for Digital 
UNIX(R), OpenVMS and Windows 3.1 platforms.

     Open Environment's Entera provides a way for companies to 
create an open, standards-based infrastructure for the enterprise in 
which to develop, deploy and manage distributed applications. Entera 
products support a wide variety of development platforms and 
programming languages, which means organizations can leverage their 
existing investment in hardware, software and developer skills while 
moving into open, distributed computing.

     Founded in 1992, Boston-based Open Environment Corporation is a 
provider of three-tiered client/server software that enables rapid 
application development across all computing platforms. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
