               DIGITAL NAMES HAMAWAKI AS CHAIRMAN AND
                        WATANABE AS PRESIDENT
               OF DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION JAPAN


MAYNARD, Mass. -- May 23, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced two appointments to the management of its Japanese 
operations.  Youji Hamawaki president of Digital Equipment 
Corporation Japan, has been appointed to chairman and representative 
director and Kuniaki Watanabe will join the company as Digital 
Japan's new president.  Both appointments will become effective July 
1, 1995.

     Watanabe, 47, comes to Digital from EDS Japan K.K. where he 
served as executive vice president and was a member of the boards of 
EDS and its affiliate company Japan Systems K.K. Previously, he held 
senior management positions at General Electric Japan, Ltd. and IBM 
Japan, Ltd. He received his bachelor's degree in Business Law from 
Sophia University in Tokyo. In his new position, he will report to 
Bobby Choonavala, Corporate vice president and president of Asia 
Pacific.

     Digital's Chairman of the Board, President and Chief Executive 
Officer Robert B. Palmer commented, "Japan represents one of the 
biggest country market opportunities for Digital's industry-leading 
technologies and services. The appointments we are announcing today 
will combine Hamawaki's experience and stature in the business 
community with Watanabe's entrepreneurial vision and drive as an 
established leader in the Japanese information technology industry. 

     "We look forward to Watanabe joining Digital and building on 
the progress we have made in Japan over the past two years under the 
leadership of Hamawaki." 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
